=== foundation ===

# React SPA Guidelines

This application’s React SPA lives under **`resources/js`**. Follow these guidelines when working on the SPA to match existing structure and conventions.

## Foundational Context

- **React** — v19
- **TypeScript** — strict mode; path alias **`@/*`** → **`./resources/js/*`** (see root `tsconfig.json`)
- **Vite** — v7 (root `package.json` scripts: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`)
- **react-router-dom** — v7 (`createBrowserRouter`, loaders, data APIs)
- **Effect** — `effect` + `Schema` from `effect` for HTTP and JSON decoding in `@/lib/apiCore` (e.g. `httpRequest`, `decodeJson`, `runEffect`, `withRetry`)
- **Tailwind CSS** — v4 (see project Tailwind rules)
- **ESLint** — v9; **Prettier** — v3

## Conventions

- Follow existing code conventions. When adding or editing SPA code, check sibling files and the same feature folder for structure, naming, and patterns.
- Use descriptive names (e.g. `hasFetchedUser`). Prefer full words over abbreviations unless widely used (e.g. `id`, `url`).
- Reuse existing components from `@/components` and feature-level components before introducing new ones.
- Use the **`@/`** path alias for all imports under `resources/js` (e.g. `@/components/ui/Button`, `@/lib/utils`).
- Use **`@/schemas/...`** for generated API/domain types and schemas (see **Types and schemas**). Do not hand-edit generated files.

=== structure ===

## Application structure

- **Entry:** [`resources/js/main.tsx`](resources/js/main.tsx) — `AuthProvider`, `RouterProvider` with [`router.tsx`](resources/js/router.tsx); theme init via `useAppearance`.
- **Shell:** [`resources/js/app.tsx`](resources/js/app.tsx) — `Sidebar` (md+), `Header` (mobile), `OfflineBanner`, `GlobalRealtimeListener`, `AuthGuard` wrapping `Outlet`, `ModalRenderer`, `Toaster`.
- **Router:** [`resources/js/router.tsx`](resources/js/router.tsx) — root layout route `/` with `App`, `errorElement: ErrorPage`; wildcard `*` → `NotFoundPage`.
- **Features:** Folders under [`resources/js/features/`](resources/js/features/) — e.g. `auth`, `game-sessions`, `home`, `profile`, plus shared [`ErrorPage`](resources/js/features/ErrorPage.tsx) / [`NotFoundPage`](resources/js/features/NotFoundPage.tsx).
- **Shared:** [`resources/js/components/`](resources/js/components/), [`resources/js/lib/`](resources/js/lib/), [`resources/js/hooks/`](resources/js/hooks/), [`resources/js/config/`](resources/js/config/) (e.g. navigation).

## Feature structure

Patterns in this repo:

- **`features/auth/routes.tsx`** — Exports `authRoutes` (`RouteObject[]`) for login, register, password flows; each auth screen sets `handle: { isAuthPage: true }`.
- **Other routes** — Declared inline in `router.tsx` (e.g. `/`, `/game-sessions/lobby`, `/profile`) or added there as the app grows.
- **Page + loader** — Co-located in the same module when used (e.g. `GameSessionsLobbyPage` + `gameSessionsLobbyLoader`, `ProfilePage` + `profileLoader`).
- **`api.ts`** per feature where needed — call through `@/lib/apiCore`; return tagged results (`_tag: 'Success'` vs error tags) from `runEffect(...)`.

=== types and schemas ===

## Types and schemas

### Generated Effect schemas (single source of truth)

- The Laravel API models request and response JSON using **Spatie Laravel Data** (`Data` classes): shared types under `app/Data`, feature requests/responses under `app/Features/**`, and PHP enums under `app/Enums`. Prefer **named `Data` DTOs** for bodies (including simple `{ message }` / `{ error }` responses) so the wire format stays explicit and versionable.
- **`php artisan effect-schema:transform`** (`michael4d45/effect-schema-generator`) scans those PHP classes and writes **Effect `Schema` modules and TypeScript** into **`resources/js/schemas`** (see root `config/effect-schema.php` for scan paths). The SPA imports them as **`@/schemas/...`** (e.g. `@/schemas/App/Data/Models/UserData`).
- The Vite plugin **`laravelDataTypes`** (see root `laravelDataTypes.ts`) runs the same Artisan command on **`buildStart`** and on HMR when files change under `app/Data/**/*.php`, `app/Features/**/*.php`, or `app/Enums/**/*.php`. After changing PHP `Data` types, rely on dev/build for regeneration, or run the Artisan command manually if needed.
- **Do not hand-edit anything under `resources/js/schemas`.** To add or change API shapes, add or update the PHP `Data` (or enum) class, then regenerate so `decodeJson` / feature APIs stay aligned.

### Using schemas in the SPA

- Prefer **`decodeJson`** (and generated schemas from `@/schemas/...`) for JSON response and request bodies in **`@/lib/apiCore`** and feature **`api.ts`** modules so decoding matches the backend contract.
- Use **type-only imports** when only types are needed: `import type { … } from '@/schemas/...'`.
- Define **props interfaces** for component props (e.g. `ButtonProps`). Extend DOM props when wrapping native elements (e.g. `React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>`).
- Rely on **TypeScript strict**; avoid `any`; handle null/undefined explicitly.

### Typical API response DTOs (for decoding)

- **`MessageResponse`** — `{ message: string }` (e.g. deletes, logout, simple notices).
- **`ErrorResponseData`** — `{ error: string }` (e.g. broadcasting auth failures).
- **`PasswordResetFailedResponseData`** — `{ message, errors }` on structured 422-style failures. Prefer decoding with the generated schema rather than ad hoc object shapes.

=== react patterns ===

## React patterns

- **Ref-forwarding:** When wrapping native elements, use `React.forwardRef` and set `displayName` where the codebase already does (e.g. `Button`).
- **Loaders:** Export async loader functions from the page module (or a dedicated module). Use `LoaderFunctionArgs` from `react-router` / `react-router-dom` when you need `params` or `request`. In the component, `useLoaderData<YourType>()`. Handle API errors in the loader (fallback data or rethrow as appropriate).
- **Data flow:** Loaders for initial route data; local `useState` for UI-only state. Use **`useAuth()`** from `@/features/auth/AuthContext` for session user and auth actions.
- **Modals:** `@/lib/modal` + `ModalRenderer`; avoid duplicating global modal chrome.
- **Toasts:** `react-hot-toast`; toaster options live in `app.tsx`.
- **URL state:** `useSearchParams` when the route should be shareable/bookmarkable for list/filter state; keep loaders aligned with the same query keys if they read the URL.

=== api and data ===

## API and data

- **Core:** `@/lib/apiCore` — `httpRequest`, `buildQueryString`, `decodeJson` with `Schema`, `runEffect`, `withRetry`, cache helpers as needed.
- **Contract with Laravel:** Treat **`@/schemas/...`** as the typed mirror of PHP `Data` DTOs. When adding an endpoint or changing a payload, extend the PHP `Data` class first, regenerate schemas, then update the feature API layer to use the new schema in **`decodeJson`** (or equivalent). Avoid inline “best guess” TypeScript types that are not backed by generated schemas.
- **Errors:** Check `result._tag`; branch on `Success` vs validation / auth / network error tags; surface messages with toasts or inline UI.
- **Auth:** `authManager` + `AuthContext` / `useAuth()`; do not duplicate token storage logic ad hoc.
- **Offline:** Respect `useOfflineBlock`, `OfflineBanner`, and related patterns when adding mutations or gated UI.

=== styling ===

## Styling (Tailwind)

- Use **Tailwind v4** utilities only (no deprecated v3-only classes). Follow project rules for spacing and theme tokens.
- Use **`cn()`** from `@/lib/utils` to merge class names.
- **Spacing:** Prefer `gap-*` in flex/grid layouts.
- **Dark mode:** Follow existing `dark:` and CSS variable patterns used in shared components.
- Reuse **`@/components/ui/*`** (`Button`, `ButtonLink`, `Form`, `FormField`, etc.).

=== routing and auth ===

## Routing and auth

- **Router:** Add or extend routes in `router.tsx` and/or feature `routes.tsx`; use `RouteObject` from `react-router-dom`.
- **Loaders:** Attach to the route that owns the data; keep them free of unrelated side effects beyond fetch/decode.
- **`AuthGuard`:** Routes are **public by default**. Mark **protected** routes with **`handle: { isProtected: true }`** (see `/profile`). **`/game-sessions/lobby`** stays public for the guard so guests can open it; the lobby API still uses session auth. Mark **auth-only pages** (login, register, etc.) with **`handle: { isAuthPage: true }`** so logged-in users are redirected home. There is no `isGuestPage` handle in this app.

=== quality and tooling ===

## Quality and tooling

- From the project root: **`npm run lint`**, **`npm run types`**, and **`npm run format`** / **`npm run format:check`** before finalizing SPA changes. Run **`npm run types`** after PHP `Data` / enum changes if Vite was not running (schemas may be stale until `effect-schema:transform` runs).

## Documentation

- Do not add new SPA README or doc files unless the user explicitly asks for them.

